---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { ONE_LINE, RECRUITER_LINE } from '../lib/how-its-built';
import { HOW_PATH, SITE_LAB } from '../lib/links';

// The launch home (docs/product.md, "Who it serves": something to click that works in a minute,
// and a sentence to repeat). The copy is a draft for the owner to edit. The two data-tour anchors are the
// home screen's tour (tour/simple.ts, HOME).
---

<Base
  title="Proof of Concept Bakery"
  description="A made-up bakery built as a real business system in Rust on Cloudflare: order with a test card, watch the kitchen, move the clock. Nothing here is real."
  screen="home"
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Proof of Concept Bakery</h1>
    <p class="statement" data-tour="home-intro">
      {ONE_LINE}
    </p>
    <p>{RECRUITER_LINE}</p>

    <section aria-labelledby="try-title" data-tour="home-links">
      <h2 id="try-title">Try it in a minute</h2>
      <ol class="try-steps">
        <li>
          <a href="/signin/">Sign in, or try it as a guest</a>. Either one makes your own sandbox: a
          private copy of the bakery, deleted tonight.
        </li>
        <li>
          Open <a href="/menu/">the menu</a> and put a loaf or a box of pastries in the cart.
        </li>
        <li>
          Check out: choose a pickup slot and pay with Stripe’s test card,{' '}
          <code>4242 4242 4242 4242</code>, with any future date and any CVC. No money moves.
        </li>
        <li>
          Find the receipt in <a href="/inbox/">the inbox</a>. The bakery holds no email address for
          anyone, so every message it sends lands there.
        </li>
        <li>
          Open <a href="/app/">the console</a>: your sandbox, the kitchen board with your order on
          it, and, once you are signed in, the clock, which you can move forward to see tomorrow.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Every screen has a tour that says what you are looking at and how to do the same from a
        terminal. <a href={HOW_PATH}>How it’s built</a> explains each technique, and{' '}
        <a href={SITE_LAB} rel="noopener">
          the lab on ihaveasegway.com
        </a>{' '}
        shows the principles behind them as simulations.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="draft">
      <strong>Nothing here is real.</strong> The bakery, its customers, their orders and their cards
      are made up, and your sandbox is deleted at 10:00 UTC every night.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
